        "text": "Annex E gives non-exhaustive examples of risks that can affect activities in a national eHealth action plan, grouped in tables by area. Leadership and governance risks include a lack of credible leaders, weak oversight, conflicting agendas and resistance to changing governance, while stakeholder risks include poor clinical engagement, sector fragmentation, unorganized stakeholders, resistance to eHealth and unmet expectations. Further tables cover resource and funding risks such as scarce skills and funds, implementation approach risks such as overly broad scope or slow delivery of benefits, and external dependencies on infrastructure, standards, reusable systems and vendor products.",
